{"url": "https://physics.indiana.edu/", "final_url": "https://physics.indiana.edu/", "status": 200, "method": "http", "fetched": "2026-10-21", "text": "Department of Physics: Indiana University Bloomington\nSkip to Content\nSkip to Main Navigation\nSkip to Search\nThe College of Arts & Sciences\nDepartment of Physics\nHome\nAbout\nDirectory\nChair's Message\nEmployment Opportunities\nVisit Us\nDirections & Building Maps\nAbout Bloomington\nUndergraduate\nPhysics B.A.\nTraditional Physics B.S.\nApplied Physics B.S.\nPhysics Minor\nHonors Program\nCourses\nAdvising\nFunding Opportunities\nScholarships & Awards\nResearch Opportunities\nStudent Experience\nCareer Preparation\nGraduate\nMaster's Degrees\nDoctoral Degrees\nAPS Bridge Program\nCourses\nAdvising\nFinancial Support\nFellowships & Awards\nStudent Experience\nCareer Preparation\nHow to Apply\nResearch\nResearch Areas\nCenters & Institutes\nAlumni & Giving\nGet Involved\nOutreach\nAnnual Community Events\nOutreach Programs\nEducational Services & Associations\nREU Program\nNews & Events\nEvents\nDepartment news\nSearch\nContact\nStudent Portal\nA community of problem solvers\nIU\u2019s Department of Physics is known for conducting world-leading research across a wide portfolio of sub-disciplines in physics. We offer a strong teaching and research environment, combining individual mentoring that is typical of a small liberal arts college with a rich variety of experiences and resources only available at a major research university.\nExplore IU Physics\nOur programs\nOur undergraduate program is excellent preparation for careers in industry and the private sector or graduate school. We offer a variety of degree options: Physics B.A., Physics B.S., Applied Physics B.S., and a Physics minor. Our comprehensive graduate program immerses students in exciting research as part of their master's or Ph.D. degree, and includes an APS-sponsored M.S.-to-Ph.D. bridge program.\nThe Physics Graduate Program will not require general or subject GRE scores for graduate applications for current applications.\nView our undergraduate programs\nView our graduate degrees\nA breadth of course offerings\nCourses in our department cover the underlying laws of nature at every scale\u2014from subatomic particles, to the emergent properties of complex materials, to the forces shaping the structure of the universe. The broad range of physics research conducted at IU is matched by an equally expansive collection of course offerings.\nLearn about undergraduate courses Learn about graduate courses\nFind support + opportunity\nOur world-class faculty foster exploration and innovation, and provide research opportunities at both the undergraduate and graduate levels. We encourage our students to gain valuable, real-world experience through internships and positions in industry, academia, or national laboratories.\nUndergraduate career preparation\nGraduate career preparation\nA hub for cutting-edge research\nNationally ranked groups in our department carry out research in particle physics, nuclear physics, astrophysics, cosmology, condensed matter physics and material science, biophysics, and accelerator physics. Research activities are channeled via institutes and centers such as the Nuclear Theory Center, the Center for Spacetime Symmetries, the Center for Exploration of Energy and Matter (CEEM), and the Quantum Science and Engineering Center.\nLearn about research\nView our research areas\nMeet our faculty\nNews\nIU scientists help unlock neutrino\u2019s secrets\nUndergraduates Shine at Physics Department\u2019s First Poster Session\nArtificial intelligence used to improve speed and accuracy of autism and ADHD diagnoses\nRead more news\nEvents\nOct\n24\nScience Fest 2026\n10 a.m.\u20144 p.m.\nOct\n27\nThe Sixth Robert E. Pollock Distinguished Lecture in Physics: Donna Strickland on \u201cTrust in Science\u201d\nStarts at 7:30 p.m.\nINDIANA MEMORIAL UNION (UNION BUILDING)\n-\nOct\n28\nColloquium: Donna Strickland on From Nonlinear Optics to High-Intensity Laser Physics\nStarts at 4 p.m.\nSWAIN HALL WEST\n-\nSee more events\nReady to take the next step?\nIncoming freshmen\nContact IU Admissions\nCurrent IU students\nContact our advisors\nProspective graduate students\nSee our application process\nFaculty + Staff + Grad Student Intranet\nDepartment of Physics social media channels\nTwitter\nFacebook\nCollege of Arts & Sciences\nDepartment of Physics\nThe College of Arts & Sciences\nThe College of Arts & Sciences\nAbout\nDirectory\nAll Faculty & Scientists\nFaculty\nAdjunct & Visiting Faculty\nResearch Scientists\nResearch Associates & Postdoctoral Fellows\nEmeriti and Retired Faculty\nPast Faculty\nStaff\nPast Staff\nRetired Staff\nGraduate Students\nFacilities & Support\nChair's Message\nEmployment Opportunities\nVisit Us\nDirections & Building Maps\nAbout Bloomington\nMusic + Entertainment\nCampus Culture & Resources\nFood & Restaurants\nSustainability\nSports & Fitness\nHousing In Bloomington\nUndergraduate\nPhysics B.A.\nTraditional Physics B.S.\nApplied Physics B.S.\nFAQs\nPhysics Minor\nHonors Program\nCourses\nAdvising\nFunding Opportunities\nScholarships & Awards\nResearch Opportunities\nStudent Experience\nCareer Preparation\nCareer Advising\nInternships\nGraduate\nMaster's Degrees\nDoctoral Degrees\nAPS Bridge Program\nCourses\nAdvising\nFinancial Support\nFellowships & Awards\nStudent Experience\nCareer Preparation\nHow to Apply\nDomestic Applications\nInternational Applications\nResearch\nResearch Areas\nAstrophysics\nAtomic Physics and Quantum Information\nBiophysics\nChemical Physics\nCondensed Matter Physics\nElementary Particle Physics\nGravitational Physics\nMathematical Physics\nNeutrino Physics\nNuclear Physics\nQuantum Information Science and Technology\nCenters & Institutes\nAlumni & Giving\nGet Involved\nOutreach\nAnnual Community Events\nOutreach Programs\nNSF Research Experience\nEducational Services & Associations\nREU Program\nNews & Events\nEv